8. Real-world senior DBA scenario questions
These are particularly important because senior-level interviews often focus on production incidents rather than textbook definitions.
Scenario	What the interviewer expects
AG secondary is disconnected	Endpoint, network, WSFC, replica health, SQL error logs
AG synchronization is suspended	Check database state, log transport, disk and network
Primary server crashes	Automatic/manual failover, quorum, recovery
Database is in SUSPECT state	Error logs, storage, DBCC CHECKDB, restore strategy
Transaction log is full	Log reuse wait, backups, long transactions, AG replication
Database migration takes too long	Backup throughput, network, log generation, parallel restore
SQL Server CPU is continuously high	Query Store, execution plans, waits, CPU-intensive queries
Application reports intermittent timeout	Blocking, network, connection pooling, resource pressure
DR site is several hours behind	Log send queue, redo queue, network bandwidth, workload
Upgrade causes performance regression	Compatibility level, Query Store, plan changes, cardinality estimator

Q52. A SQL Server database migration fails halfway through. What is your approach?
- Identify the failure point.
- Check backup integrity and restore sequence.
- Verify LSN continuity for log backups.
- Check available storage.
- Check SQL Server error logs.
- Resume from the last successfully restored backup if possible.
- Otherwise restart according to the migration recovery plan.
